  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 238 AM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nLow pressure aloft slides through the region today and tonight and \nthen passes east tomorrow. Sfc high pressure continues to build with \ncool NE winds today. Highs will be much cooler and more Fall like \ntoday in the mid 70s to low 80s. Plenty of cloud cover will hang \naround (especially up north) until the low shifts east tomorrow. \nThis will help keep temperatures down. \n\nRidging aloft builds over the Midwest Thursday, Friday, and into the \nweekend with a nor'easter forming off the coast of New England and \nthe Mid Atlantic states. The EC and GFS both hint at some energy \nrounding the ridge and bringing some precip chances to SEMO and \nsouthern IL on Sunday. However, NBM is currently essentially dry \nover the weekend for now. Temperatures look to then warm up into the \nmid-upper 80s for the start of the work week, but there are\nstill some decent model discrepancies to work out.",
